Title: What They Called Recovery
Credit: Animated feature screenplay — source-developed working scene
Author: Christopher Kokkinos
Draft date: 2026-10-10
Status: Independent screenplay development under DEC-0019; refinements during production

INT. NORTH CAFE, CLOCK SQUARE - TUESDAY - DAY

A waitress sets four drinks down in the wrong places. Voss swaps them. Zoe orders chips, no mayonnaise. Her backpack stays between her feet, beside Elias rather than across from him.

VOSS
Voss.

VALE
Vale.

ZOE
I know. Reyes.

Vale grips her cup.

VOSS
We're not here to avenge him. We terminated Mac's contract.

ELIAS
He agreed?

VOSS
No. We won't pursue Zoe, her folder or drive. He'll replace us.

Elias explains buyer, false family destination and Cain's separate interest. Zoe answers questions about her own file herself. Jackie stays unnamed; coercion remains their inference.

VALE
We've seen this delegated language on recoveries. Some real. We didn't know enough to separate the others.

ZOE
That's useful.

VALE
Culpable.

Voss slides a marked intermediary sheet beneath the newspaper: payments, number forwarding, vehicle supplier and certifying solicitor. Meridian appears in Zoe's folder. Verified entries are marked, not assumed universal.

VOSS
The next brief makes him the abductor, you coerced or unstable, the drive stolen property.

Zoe sets down a chip.

VOSS
We need to know you're here by choice.

VALE
You and me at the counter. Elias visible. Thirty seconds.

ZOE
No. You decide which room makes me truthful. Everyone who decided something about me first moved me away from the person who might disagree.

VOSS
Would he let you leave?

ZOE
He doesn't own the answer. He stops me when danger is immediate. He explains when it isn't. Sometimes he gets it wrong.

ELIAS
Frequently.

VALE
We remain here.

Voss nods. The meeting continues at the same table.

Vale notices the fruit seller looking beyond a customer. New men near the flowers and pharmacy. A coat folded over an arm in clear weather. She doesn't turn twice.

VALE
Voss. Two confirmed. Not ours.

Elias flattens his hand on the newspaper. Zoe stops chewing.

VALE
The incoming watch. Number forwarding.

The intermediary sheet lies between them. Their invitation has reached somebody else.
